# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# whos-accountable — onboarded 2026-10-17 at James's request on music-miles#1
#
#   "Can you onboard these projects onto kit even if you don't start working on them yet"
#
# The empty repo `climate-accountability` appears to be the same idea, so this
# corpus is named for the repo that holds the work: whos-accountable.
#
# Read at whos-accountable@dev: a .NET scoring core (ScoreEngine, DatasetLoader,
# a synthetic cohort and a golden-file test) and docs/DESIGN.md. There is no web
# API and no frontend yet.
#
#   DEFINED   — his words on whos-accountable#1 (the idea, plus his scope answers:
#               UK-first, companies-only, read-only v1, sentiment and individuals
#               in the backlog). Cites the issue.
#   INFERRED  — what the code or the bot's own backlog issues (#4-#15) state.
#               Each is `review unreviewed`: it shows in Proposed, and he can
#               deny it. Numbers are copied from ScoringConstants.cs.
#
# Nothing here is wired to a test map yet; `kit check whos-accountable` names
# what is not built.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

feature FEAT-LEADERBOARD "Leaderboards of the worst offenders and the top do-gooders"
  stage development
feature FEAT-SCORING "The credibility score: a published formula over open data"
  stage ui
feature FEAT-DATA "Datasets and sourcing"
  stage development
feature FEAT-COMPANY "Company pages"
  stage logic
feature FEAT-BACKLOG "Later: other countries, individuals, sentiment"
  stage problem


# ═══ DEFINED — whos-accountable#1 ═══

# kit.notes.md#2026-10-26-2252, "Getting who's accountable can't be read error": a missing space
# after BEH-LEADER-1 below stopped this file parsing on hosted. Fixed in kit#478.
# LEADER-1/2 and SCORE-5 read as built until 2026-10-26 (they predate `pending`); the repo has no
# frontend. The leaderboards are paused by the agent while the project is parked (BEH-BACKLOG-1).
behaviour BEH-LEADER-1 "The core of the app is a leaderboard of the worst offenders"
  in FEAT-LEADERBOARD
  layer ux
  source defined whos-accountable#1
  review approved
  priority 1
  pending
  paused
  actor visitor
  when opens page:WorstOffenders
  then sees region:Leaderboard
  contract "The core part will be company and individual leaderboards. Showing both ways - worse offenders leaderboard and top do gooders"
  contract the aim is visibility: "keep billionairs and corporations accountable for their actions"

behaviour BEH-LEADER-2 "A second leaderboard shows the top do-gooders"
  in FEAT-LEADERBOARD
  layer ux
  source defined whos-accountable#1
  priority 1
  pending
  paused
  actor visitor
  when opens page:TopDoGooders
  then sees region:Leaderboard
  contract the same companies, ordered the other way round

behaviour BEH-SCOPE-1 "Version 1 covers UK companies only"
  in FEAT-LEADERBOARD
  layer technical
  source defined whos-accountable#1
  priority 1
  actor visitor
  contract "keep it simple with uk": the US, EU and global come later (BEH-BACKLOG-1)
  contract individuals are out of v1 and sit in the backlog (BEH-BACKLOG-2)

behaviour BEH-SCOPE-2 "Version 1 is read-only: no accounts, no contributions"
  in FEAT-LEADERBOARD
  layer technical
  source defined whos-accountable#1
  priority 1
  actor visitor
  contract "Maybe read only v1, sentiment as a backlog": a visitor reads, and nothing a visitor does changes the data


# ═══ INFERRED — design doc, backlog issues, code ═══

behaviour BEH-SCORE-1 "A company's composite is a 0-100 score from published pillars with published weights"
  in FEAT-SCORING
  layer technical
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.WhosAccountable.Abstractions/Constants/ScoringConstants.cs:21
  review approved
  priority 4
  actor visitor
  provides pillar:Emissions.weight = 0.40
  provides pillar:Violations.weight = 0.60
  contract weights live in code as named constants, so changing how companies are scored is a reviewed diff
  contract scores are rounded to 2 decimal places so results are reproducible

behaviour BEH-SCORE-2 "The emissions sub-score falls as emissions intensity rises"
  in FEAT-SCORING
  layer technical
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.WhosAccountable.Abstractions/Constants/ScoringConstants.cs:35
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor visitor
  contract score = 100 * e^(-intensity / 200), intensity in tCO2e per million pounds of revenue
  contract the v1 values are chosen for a sensible spread, not calibrated against the full cohort

behaviour BEH-SCORE-3 "The violations sub-score falls with fines, incidents and discharge hours"
  in FEAT-SCORING
  layer technical
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.WhosAccountable.Abstractions/Constants/ScoringConstants.cs:40
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor visitor
  contract harm = 1.0 per million pounds of fines + 0.5 per incident + 1.0 per 1,000 hours of sewage or storm-overflow discharge
  contract score = 100 * e^(-harm / 5); a company with no recorded enforcement scores 100

behaviour BEH-SCORE-4 "Missing data is unknown, never a neutral 50"
  in FEAT-SCORING
  layer technical
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.WhosAccountable.Services/Scoring/ScoreEngine.cs:91
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor visitor
  contract a pillar with no data is excluded and the composite is renormalised over the pillars that have a value
  contract a company with no data at all stays unknown: it is not crowned a do-gooder by its own absence
  contract unknown composites sort last, whichever direction the leaderboard runs

behaviour BEH-SCORE-5 "A methodology page explains the formula, the weights and every source"
  in FEAT-SCORING
  layer ux
  source inferred docs/DESIGN.md:1
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  pending
  actor visitor
  when opens page:Methodology
  then sees region:Formula
  contract the credibility of the whole app rests on this page (bot's own framing on whos-accountable#1)

behaviour BEH-SCORE-6 "A golden-file test pins the whole leaderboard over a synthetic cohort"
  in FEAT-SCORING
  layer technical
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.WhosAccountable.Tests/GoldenLeaderboardTests.cs:1
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor maintainer
  contract any change to the formula shows up as a visible diff in the leaderboard
  contract the cohort is synthetic, so there is no risk of a wrong real figure

behaviour BEH-DATA-1 "Only open-government data feeds the composite: UK ETS emissions and EA/Ofwat enforcement"
  in FEAT-DATA
  layer technical
  source inferred whos-accountable#9
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor maintainer
  contract CDP, SBTi and InfluenceMap cannot be folded into the score without written permission (licence audit, whos-accountable#9)
  contract the permission emails are tracked in whos-accountable#11

behaviour BEH-DATA-2 "Every record carries its source link and retrieval date"
  in FEAT-DATA
  layer technical
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.WhosAccountable.DomainModels/Models/SourceRef.cs:1
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor maintainer
  contract "every number links to its source" (bot's proposal on whos-accountable#1)

behaviour BEH-DATA-3 "The first real dataset replaces the synthetic fixtures: about 150 UK-linked companies, hand-curated"
  in FEAT-DATA
  layer technical
  source inferred whos-accountable#13
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor maintainer
  pending
  contract data is versioned in the repo as data-as-code
  contract scheduled refresh (whos-accountable#7) and SECR full-text extraction (whos-accountable#8) are separate, later

behaviour BEH-COMPANY-1 "A company page shows its score, its pillar sub-scores and the evidence behind them"
  in FEAT-COMPANY
  layer ux
  source inferred whos-accountable#15
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor visitor
  pending
  when opens page:Company
  then sees region:PillarScores

behaviour BEH-COMPANY-2 "Restricted sources appear on a company page as attributed third-party signals, outside the score"
  in FEAT-COMPANY
  layer ux
  source inferred whos-accountable#9
  review unreviewed
  priority 5
  actor visitor
  pending
  contract each signal credits its source and links to it; CDP is link-only until licensed
  contract if ads ever go live, even this needs the permission emails to have landed first

behaviour BEH-API-1 "A read-only web API serves the leaderboards and company pages"
  in FEAT-LEADERBOARD
  layer technical
  source inferred whos-accountable#14
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor visitor
  pending
  contract a WebApi with an EF read model; there is no API in the repo yet


# ═══ BACKLOG — the bot's issues, lowest priority ═══

behaviour BEH-BACKLOG-1 "Coverage expands from the UK to the US, then the EU, then global"
  in FEAT-BACKLOG
  layer technical
  source defined whos-accountable#1
  priority 3
  needs-context "Restart whos-accountable now, or keep it parked until snip-it ships? I keep it parked."
  actor visitor
  pending
  contract "create an issue to expand to uk + us and then maybe eu and global later" (issue whos-accountable#4)

behaviour BEH-BACKLOG-2 "Individuals, such as billionaires, get leaderboard entries"
  in FEAT-BACKLOG
  layer technical
  source defined whos-accountable#1
  priority 3
  needs-context "Restart whos-accountable now, or keep it parked until snip-it ships? I keep it parked."
  actor visitor
  pending
  contract "Fine to park maybe also backlog": parked pending a defamation review (whos-accountable#5)

behaviour BEH-BACKLOG-3 "A clearly separate public-sentiment layer sits beside the evidence-based score"
  in FEAT-BACKLOG
  layer ux
  source defined whos-accountable#1
  priority 3
  needs-context "Restart whos-accountable now, or keep it parked until snip-it ships? I keep it parked."
  actor visitor
  pending
  contract "sentiment as a backlog" (whos-accountable#6)
  contract sentiment never feeds the evidence score: crowd voting invites brigading and defamation risk
